# Mesa patch series for GFX1013 (BC-250), applied in order against
# pristine mesa-26.2.0-rc3 with `git apply` / `patch -p1`.
#
# Comment out a line with '#' to skip that patch. 0001 is the compute
# fix and is required; 0002 and 0003 are optional features. 0003
# requires 0002.
#
# 0002/0003 enable mesh/task shading on GFX1013. The user-visible
# feature path stays disabled unless 0004 sees RADV_GFX103=1 at
# runtime. Mesh shaders work (FF7 Rebirth tested); task shaders are
# still not working correctly — games that rely on task shaders may
# render incorrectly, hang or crash. Do not export RADV_GFX103=1
# globally; enable it only per-game.
#
# 0004 adds an opt-in RADV_GFX103=1 env var to promote GFX1013 to the
# GFX10.3 software path. Safe by itself — only activates when the user
# explicitly sets the env var. Requires 0002/0003 to be useful.
#
# 0005 selectively reassociates the NIR fallback for the signed 4x8
# dot product (sdot_4x8_iadd). When the accumulator is a constant,
# keeps the balanced tree (avoids register pressure); otherwise uses
# the right-leaning chain for fewer instructions. Always active
# regardless of environment variables (from dmorazasanchez/bc250-fsr4 v2).
0001-gfx1013-compute-queue-fix.patch
0002-gfx1013-mesh-task-shaders.patch
0003-gfx1013-taskmesh-queries.patch
0004-radv-gfx103.patch
0005-bc250-fsr4-selective-sdot4x8.patch
